  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Social Protection phase II, Strengthened resilience and livelihood - Social Protection - support to livelihoods &amp; Financial Inclusion (new) 2025-2028</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Social Protection phase II, Strengthened resilience and livelihood</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Insatsens syfte &#xe4;r att st&#xe4;rka Etiopiens m&#xf6;jlighet att forts&#xe4;tta sitt ambiti&#xf6;sa arbete inom social trygghet vilket inkluderar utveckling av ny policy och system samt att st&#xe4;rka genomf&#xf6;randet av st&#xf6;d till utsatta grupper s&#xe5;som internflyktingar och barn samt i utvecklingen av nya innovativa st&#xf6;dprogram. Insatsen f&#xf6;rv&#xe4;ntas h&#xe4;rigenom bidra till konkreta resultat f&#xf6;r att minska flerdimensionell fattigdom i Etiopien. Sida har valt att kanalisera ett st&#xf6;d om MSEK 75 via UNICEF under 2025-2018 och till programmet Social trygghet &#x2013; st&#xe4;rkt resiliens och f&#xf6;rs&#xf6;rjning.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The objective of the intervention is to strengthen Ethiopia&apos;s capacity to continue its ambitious work in social protection, including the development of new policies and systems, and to strengthen the implementation of support to vulnerable groups such as IDPs and children, as well as in the development of new innovative programmes. The intervention is expected to contribute to concrete results in reducing multidimensional poverty in Ethiopia. Sida has chosen to channel the support, MSEK 75, through UNICEF 2025-2028  to the programme &#x201c;Social Protection - Strengthening Resilience and Livelihoods&#x201d;.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The overall objective of the programme is:

to establish effective systems for holistic social protection to promote empowerment and resilience of the most vulnerable women and children in rural and urban Ethiopia

The specific objectives of the program are:

I. To create an enabling environment, enhance the legal frameworks and national policies and the national capacity to deliver social protection programmes,

II. To increase shock-responsiveness through enhanced coverage and effective linkages to urban and rural safety net and HCT interventions,

III. To facilitate and strengthen socio-economic inclusion through improved access to economic opportunities and skills development, for both PSNP and other social assistance recipients,

IV. To enhance service linkages through the cash plus care approach and generate evidence from interventions to enhance the effectiveness of the PSNP/UPSNJP with a particular focus on child-sensitive social protection.

The core proposed programme activities are:

- support strengthening capacity of MoWSA, its regional and respective woreda offices, to implement cash plus care and support programs to support implementation of the permanent and temporary direct support components of the rural and urban PSNP, 

- support strengthening capacity of MoWSA, regional bureuas and respective woreda office for shock responsive social protection programming 

- support the capacity of MoWSA for evidence-based planning, policy dialogue, formulation, revision, implementation, and monitoring of holistic, child-disability sensitive, gender transformative, financially inclusive and resilience building social protection systems.</narrative>
  </description>
